{
 "note": "System 6.0.8 from the Legacy CD's 800K set, all four floppies attached as disks (the Installer finds each one mounted, no swapping): the Installer on System Tools, opened in the Finder (System 6 has no bridge: names selected, Command-O), Customize onto the blank disk: System software for any Macintosh, software for all Apple printers, AppleShare (workstation), AppleTalk Responder and 32-Bit QuickDraw (Shift-clicked), so the disk carries Color and Monitors and boots the SE and the IIci alike. Then the floppies' own utilities copied to the top of the disk in the Finder: Apple HD SC Setup, Disk First Aid (Utilities 1), Apple File Exchange, Font/DA Mover with its Fonts and Desk Accessories, MacroMaker (Utilities 2), TeachText (System Tools). Run on the IIci (colour, 68030) from the hand-made 6.0.8 disk; first boot from the new disk alone.",
